.TH BUILDBOT 1 "April 2026" "arch\-native" "User Commands"
.\" ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.SH NAME
buildbot \- arch\-native package build daemon and CLI
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B buildbot
.I COMMAND
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B buildbot
.RB [ \-\-config
.IR file ]
.RB [ \-\-debug ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B buildbot
is the daemon and CLI for
.BR arch\-native ,
a self\-hosted build system that rebuilds installed Arch (or Artix) Linux
packages from source with CPU\-optimised compiler flags, signs the resulting
packages with GPG, and publishes them as a local pacman repository.
.PP
Invoked without a
.I COMMAND
it starts the build daemon.
Invoked with a command it runs the CLI and exits immediately.
.SH COMMANDS
.SS status
Show service state, the package currently being built, queue and failure
counts, and stats from the most recent poll cycle.
.SS doctor
Verify that all required paths exist, JSON state files are valid, the GPG
home has correct permissions (0700), and the chroot pacman keyring is
initialised.
Safe to run while the service is active.
.SS fsck [\-\-dry\-run] [\-v] [\-\-force]
Verify and repair consistency between
.IR built.json ,
the pacman repo database, and physical
.I .pkg.tar.zst
files.
Detects and fixes divergences caused by a SIGKILL or interrupted build cycle.
Also runs automatically at daemon startup.
Requires the service to be stopped first.
.TP
.B \-\-dry\-run
Report issues without making any changes (exits 1 if any are found).
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
Also print packages that are fully consistent.
.TP
.B \-\-force
Run even if the service is active (unsafe).
.SS built [\-n \fIN\fR]
List packages successfully rebuilt by arch\-native, newest first.
.TP
.BI \-n " N"
Limit output to the
.I N
most recent entries (default: all).
.SS logs \fIPKG\fR [\-f]
Print the latest build log for
.IR PKG .
.TP
.BR \-f ", " \-\-follow
Follow the log in real time (equivalent to
.BR "tail \-f" ).
Useful while a build is in progress.
.SS queue [\-n \fIN\fR]
List the pending build queue.
.TP
.BI \-n " N"
Limit output to the first
.I N
entries (default: 25).
.SS failed [\-n \fIN\fR]
List failed builds with failure reason and retry count.
.TP
.BI \-n " N"
Limit output to the first
.I N
entries (default: all).
.SS retry \fIPKG\fR [\-\-all] [\-\-dry\-run]
Re\-queue failed package(s) for another build attempt.
Requires the service to be stopped first.
.TP
.B \-\-all
Re\-queue every failed package.
.TP
.B \-\-dry\-run
Show what would be re\-queued without writing.
.SS clear \fIPKG\fR [\-\-all] [\-\-dry\-run]
Remove package(s) from the failed list without re\-queuing them.
Requires the service to be stopped first.
.TP
.B \-\-all
Clear the entire failed list.
.TP
.B \-\-dry\-run
Show what would be cleared without writing.
.SS sync [\-\-reset] [\-\-dry\-run]
Diff the installed package list against
.I built.json
and queue any new or updated packages.
Requires the service to be stopped first.
.TP
.B \-\-reset
Clear the existing queue first, then rebuild from scratch.
.TP
.B \-\-dry\-run
Show what would be queued without writing.
.SS init
Initialise a new arch\-native installation: create the directory layout
under
.IR /var/lib/arch\-native/ ,
build the clean devtools chroot, initialise the pacman keyring, and
set up the GPG home directory for the build user.
Safe to re\-run \(em skips steps already complete.
After running
.BR init ,
generate the signing key manually (see
.IR /usr/share/doc/arch\-native/README.md
or the project README for the
.B gpg \-\-gen\-key
invocation).
.SS why \fIPKG\fR
Explain in plain English why
.I PKG
is in its current state.
Useful for diagnosing why a package is missing from the repo or has not been built.
Possible states include:
.TP
.B built
Package has been rebuilt at the current version.
.TP
.BR failed " / " stalled
Build failed; output includes the failure reason and retry count.
A stalled package has exceeded the automatic retry threshold and requires manual
intervention with
.BR "buildbot retry" .
.TP
.B pending
Package is queued for an upcoming build.
.TP
.B pending_upstream
The installed version is ahead of the PKGBUILD in the configured tiers.
The package will be released automatically once the upstream tier catches up.
Run
.B buildbot sync
to force a re-scan.
.TP
.B ineligible
Automatically excluded:
.BR arch=any ,
Haskell packages, or a package whose pkgbase is blacklisted.
.TP
.B blacklisted
Explicitly listed in
.IR blacklist .
.TP
.B not\ found
No PKGBUILD found in any configured tier (AUR packages, binary packages).
.SS "patch {create|show|check|status|backfill} \fIPKG\fR"
Manage local PKGBUILD patches stored in
.IR /var/lib/arch\-native/pkgbuilds/local/ .
.TP
.BI "patch create " PKG " [\-\-force]"
Resolve the upstream PKGBUILD for
.I PKG
(using
.BR repo_priority ),
open it in
.BR $EDITOR ,
and save the diff as a local patch.
.B \-\-force
overwrites an existing patch with a fresh copy of upstream.
.TP
.BI "patch show " PKG
Print the local patch for
.IR PKG .
.TP
.BI "patch check " "PKG " | " \-\-all"
Verify that the local patch for
.I PKG
(or all patches with
.BR \-\-all )
still applies cleanly against the current upstream PKGBUILD.
With
.BR \-\-all ,
also reports patches for packages that are no longer installed
.RI ( orphaned )
so they can be removed.
.PP
Patches created with
.B patch create
embed the upstream pkgver and pkgrel at the time of writing.
If the upstream version has since moved,
.B patch check
reports the patch as
.B review
(applies cleanly but may be stale or redundant) rather than
.BR ok .
This catches cases where upstream silently fixed the issue the patch was
addressing.
.TP
.B "patch status"
Recompute patch health and publish
.I patch\-status.json
into the repo directory, where nginx serves it alongside the package database.
Clients read this file via
.BR native\-sync ,
which prints a one\-line summary of how many patches are ok, need review, or
have failed.
The daemon refreshes this file at startup and once per
.B upstream_check_interval
automatically; run this command to refresh it on demand.
.TP
.B "patch backfill"
Stamp existing patches that lack a version header with the current upstream
pkgver and pkgrel, establishing a baseline so future upstream drift is reported
as
.BR review .
Patches that already have a header are left untouched.
Useful once after upgrading to a version of arch\-native that records patch
versions.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-config " file"
Path to the configuration file.
Default:
.IR /etc/arch\-native.conf .
.TP
.B \-\-debug
Enable verbose (DEBUG\-level) logging.
Daemon mode only.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/arch\-native.conf
Main configuration file.
.TP
.I /var/lib/arch\-native/built.json
Record of every package successfully rebuilt, with version and timestamp.
.TP
.I /var/lib/arch\-native/pending.json
The build queue.
.TP
.I /var/lib/arch\-native/failed.json
Packages that failed to build, with failure reason and retry count.
.TP
.I /var/lib/arch\-native/in_progress.json
Package currently being built; re\-inserted at the front of the queue on
daemon restart for crash recovery.
.TP
.I /var/lib/arch\-native/metrics.json
Last\-cycle statistics (succeeded, failed, skipped counts and timestamps).
.TP
.I /var/lib/arch\-native/logs/<pkg>/
Per\-package build logs, one file per build attempt.
LTO\-retry runs are saved as
.IR YYYYMMDD\-HHMMSS\-nolto.log .
.TP
.I /var/lib/arch\-native/pkgbuilds/local/<pkg>/<pkg>.patch
Local PKGBUILD patches managed by
.BR "buildbot patch" .
.SH EXAMPLES
Check the current build state:
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
buildbot status
.EE
.RE
.PP
Follow the build log for firefox as it builds:
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
buildbot logs firefox \-f
.EE
.RE
.PP
Re\-queue a single failed package:
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
sudo systemctl stop arch\-native
sudo buildbot retry networkmanager
sudo systemctl start arch\-native
.EE
.RE
.PP
Rebuild the pending queue after a large package sync:
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
sudo systemctl stop arch\-native
sudo buildbot sync \-\-reset
sudo systemctl start arch\-native
.EE
.RE
.PP
Create a local patch to fix a build failure:
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
sudo buildbot patch create xvidcore
.EE
.RE
.PP
Diagnose why a package has not been built:
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
buildbot why firefox
.EE
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR pacman (8),
.BR makechrootpkg (1),
.BR makepkg (8),
.BR repo\-add (8)
